    "question": {
      ":question/id": "671810fd-a971-5119-a687-026670ace5f8",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int_{1}^{2}\\sech 6x\\tanh 6x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=6x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. When $x=1$, $u=6$; when $x=2$, $u=12$.\n\nUsing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\sech u=-\\sech u\\tanh u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_1^2\\sech(6x)\\tanh(6x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{6}\\int_{6}^{12}\\sech u\\tanh u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{6}[-\\sech u]_{6}^{12} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{6}(\\sech 6-\\sech 12).\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[1,2]$, and the result is positive because $\\sech u$ decreases for $u>0$.",
